  >>> i.shape.as_list()
  [3]

  This is the opposite of stack.

  >>> x = tf.stack([i, j, k, l], axis=1)

  More generally if you have a tensor of shape `(A, B, C, D)`:

  >>> A, B, C, D = [2, 3, 4, 5]
